{
 "answers": {
  "whyIntroduced": "The deck and its two hanger posts were added on 2026-09-12 as the \"vented lower shelf for motor regulator\" for the Pololu D24V150F5 servo regulator, in the version that kept a 2S battery in the original back bay and moved both regulators into the torso (hardware-design-20260912/whole-robot-20260912/assembly/README.md line 5; ../README.md lines 3, 24, 65; assembly/build_compact_battery.py lines 23-34). Neither regulator is in the current wall-powered build. On 2026-10-09 the DFR1202 took the battery bay (PROJECT-CONTEXT.json current_build.powerbank_trial_20261008.userDecision) and the OpenRB-150 moved onto the empty deck (guide/print/release-V1.6/evidence/openrb_tray-change.json reason). microduck-sim is not tracked in git, so no commit exists.",
  "positionReasonable": "The power path (DFR1202 in the old battery bay, J and 10 A fuse in the rear bay, XT30 at the lower back) is on the back, where upstream puts it, and does not use the deck. The deck now carries only the OpenRB tray. It hangs up to 13.4 mm below the original part along the inner edge of the shin path; every adopted-frame approach under 2 mm lands on that added material, while the original upstream shape stays >= 3.91 mm (left) and 4.79 mm (right) away. Balance does not need it. Acceptable at nominal timing; no margin for a 40 ms sensor delay.",
  "clearances": "See sides.*: final controller left support 1.68 mm / tray 2.92 mm; right support 0.00 mm (3 contact frames, 0.68 mm3) / tray 1.46 mm, all in phase1-candidate-old0-sensor40.json during the stop (t 25.58-25.96 s). Without the 40 ms sensor delay no frame is under 2 mm (closest measured 4.55 mm left, 3.45 mm right). Joint caps = MJCF ranges; minimum over them is 0.00 mm (they contain the walking envelope grid, which reaches 0.00 mm to support, tray and board on both sides).",
  "trimOrRelocation": "Not needed at nominal timing. For the 40 ms case a trim cannot reach 2 mm: the right post would keep 1.84 of 9.6 mm2 and the deck edge would be cut to |y| 16.3 inside the tray footprint, with the tray still 1.46 mm away. Smallest candidate corner15-deck19 (77.5 mm3, changes the already-printed support, hand-fileable) clears the left (1.68 -> 2.21 mm) but not the right (0.00 -> 0.06 mm). A relocation that clears the 40 ms case changes the support and the tray (hangers to x -59.1..-51.1, deck and tray narrowed to about |y| 16 at x -38..-22) or removes the deck and moves the OpenRB; it needs Shawn's confirmation.",
  "recommendedAction": "Keep the printed support unchanged; measure the real sensor delay before free walking; in the guide's back leg-clearance check also watch the right post front-outer corner; if the delay is near 40 ms or rubbing appears, choose one of the two redesigns. Guide steps.py line 846 should be corrected by its owner: for the final controller the right shin touches the support, the left stays 1.68 mm away and its tray gap is 2.92 mm."
 },
 "frame": "robot frame, mm: x forward, y left, z up (MuJoCo trunk_base); print frame = robot frame + 57.5 mm in z",
